course: dictionary
lesson: 268
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Amber is a good example. «Trapped in amber» is about a stone, but «an amber light» is about a traffic light.
explain: Ask yourself what amber is doing in the sentence. In «An amber weather warning means bad weather is likely», the words weather warning tell you amber is a level of warning, not a colour or a stone. Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Amber can also be a colour. It is a warm orange-yellow, like honey, so «amber eyes» are golden-brown or honey-coloured eyes. The same word can mean a stone, a colour and a traffic light, so always check the clues.
fact: Amber is a word with more than one meaning.
fact: «Amber» can mean a warm orange-yellow colour, like honey.
fact: «Amber» can mean the traffic light between red and green, which means get ready to stop.
fact: Amber is a hard, see-through stone made from hardened tree sap, and insects have been trapped inside it for millions of years.
fact: In UK weather warnings, amber is a medium level, below red, which is the highest.
exercise: «An amber weather warning means bad weather is likely and people should be ready.» In this sentence, what does amber mean? | A hard golden stone from ancient trees | A green light to go | *A medium-level warning: be ready, but it is not the top level | Sunny and warm weather
exercise: «In Jurassic Park, scientists find dinosaur blood in a mosquito trapped in amber.» In this sentence, what is amber? | *A hard golden stone made from tree sap | A weather warning | A colour, like a yellow sky | A traffic light
exercise: In weather news, which warning is the highest? | *Red | Snow | Amber | Sunny
test: «Amber eyes» are eyes with what colour? | Dark black and shiny | Shut tight | *A warm orange-yellow colour, like honey | Very tired and red
test: What is amber made from? | Melted ice | *Hardened tree sap | Painted clay | Sand from the sea
exam: A driver sees the amber light at a junction; what should they do? | Speed up to get through before it turns red | *Slow down and stop if it is safe | Close their eyes | Turn off the engine and wait
